    <system:String x:Key="BW_Status_Error">Limits not active: {0}</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="BW_PageSubtitle">Limit the whole PC or single apps — measured and enforced at the packet level</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="BW_WholePcTitle">Whole-PC speed limit</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="BW_WholePcDesc">Applies to every app together on all network adapters • slide left to slow down • far left = no internet for the whole PC • far right = unlimited</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="BW_AppRulesTitle">Per-app limits &amp; blocks</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="BW_AppRulesEmpty">No app rules yet — open Network Monitor, click an app, then drag its Down/Up sliders or press the block button at the end of its row.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="BW_Remove">Remove</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="BW_Unblock">Unblock</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="BW_ResetAll">Reset all</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="BW_ResetAllConfirm">Remove every app limit, every app block and the whole-PC limit?</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="BW_BlockedPermanent">Blocked (firewall)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="BW_NowSpeed">now ↓{0}  ↑{1}</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="BW_HowTitle">How it works</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="BW_HowText" xml:space="preserve">• Whole PC: drag the sliders above; all apps together never exceed this speed (Mbps, like your internet plan).&#x0a;• Per app: Network Monitor → click an app → drag Down/Up (KB/s or MB/s). All processes of that app share one limit.&#x0a;• Block an app: press ⛔ at the end of its row in Network Monitor. Live connections are cut at once and a Windows Firewall rule keeps it blocked even after WinXTools is closed.&#x0a;• Speed limits work while WinXTools is open (minimized is fine). With no limits the engine only watches traffic and adds no latency to games.&#x0a;• If a game anti-cheat (e.g. FACEIT, Vanguard) complains about the WinDivert driver, close WinXTools before playing.</system:String>
