    <system:String x:Key="Ram_OpStandby">Entire cache (standby list)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_OpStandbyDesc">Releases all cached files and programs, like ISLC. Right afterwards apps and games read from disk again, so they may load a little slower.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_OpCombine">Combine identical pages</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_OpCombineDesc">Windows keeps identical memory pages only once (Windows 10 and later). Uses the CPU heavily for a few seconds.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_OpFileCache">System file cache</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_OpFileCacheDesc">Moves Windows' own file cache out of active memory. Windows may have to read some files from disk again.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_OpTrim">Trim background apps</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_OpTrimDesc">Moves the memory of background apps that have done nothing for at least 2 minutes out of RAM. They may stutter for a moment when you switch back. Never touches the app you're using, WinXTools, Windows processes or services — and the automatic mode never does this.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_IncludedInEntireCache">Already included in “Entire cache”</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_NeverTrim">Never trim these programs (separate with commas):</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_NeverTrimInvalid">Not saved – not a valid program name: {0}</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_NeverTrimTooMany">Only the first {0} names are kept.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_NeverTrimSaved">Saved – {0} program(s) will never be trimmed.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_AutoDesc">Checks memory every 5 seconds and only does what measurably helps: writes out pending changes and merges identical memory pages. It never trims your programs. When the programs themselves hold the memory, or Windows gets close to running out, it tells you which ones instead.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_AutoOnLoadDesc">While memory stays at or above this: pending changes are written to disk when there are enough of them, and identical pages are merged when that paid off before — never during a full-screen game or video. “What to clean” applies only to “Clean memory now”.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_AutoOnLowFree">When free memory runs low (ISLC style)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_AutoOnLowFreeDesc">Releases the entire cache when free memory is below the first value while the cache is at least the second.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_FreeBelow">Free memory below</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_CacheAtLeast">Cache at least</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_AutoCooldown">Wait after the last cleanup at least</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_Minutes">{0} min</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Ram_AutoNoTrigger">Turn on at least one condition, otherwise nothing is cleaned automatically.</system:String>
