    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_SmartDone">Arranged {0:N0} files ({1}) in {2}.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_SmartNothing">Nothing to move — these programs' files are already in one piece near the front of the drive.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_SmartFailed">Couldn't arrange the files (Windows error {0}).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_SmartSomeSkipped">{0:N0} files couldn't be moved (in use or changed meanwhile) and were left as they were.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_SmartStopping">Stopping — finishing the piece being moved (a moment at most)…</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_StopPower">Stopped because the PC switched to battery power. Every file is whole — plug in and start again to continue.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_StopRemoval">Stopped because Windows was asked to remove the drive. Every file is whole, and the drive can be removed now.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_StopGone">The drive was disconnected while it was working. The file system keeps every file whole; when you plug it in again and Windows offers to check it, let it.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_StopUserActive">Paused because you started using the PC — it carries on another time the PC is idle.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_StopUser">Stopped. Every file is whole — the ones already moved are in their new place.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_Blocked" xml:space="preserve">WinXTools won't start on {0} right now:&#x0a;&#x0a;{1}</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_UnplugNote">This is a removable (USB) drive: don't unplug it until it has finished. To take it out early, press Stop first — or use Safely Remove: WinXTools stops and lets go of the drive by itself.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_IssueDirty">The drive has file system errors. Run "chkdsk {0}: /f" first — moving files on a damaged file system could make it worse.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_IssueFailing">The drive reports that it is failing. Copy your files somewhere else first — moving data around now puts extra strain on it.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_IssueWarning">The drive reports a health warning. Back up your important files first.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_IssueBattery">The PC is running on battery. Plug it in first — if the battery ran out half-way, the drive would lose power suddenly.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_IssueNoFlushBlock">This drive keeps written data in a cache that can't be emptied on request, so unplugging it or a power cut could lose the last writes. WinXTools won't move files on it.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_IssueNoFlush">This drive keeps written data in a cache that can't be emptied on request: keep it connected and powered until it has finished.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_IssueFlushOff">Windows is set not to flush this drive's write cache (Device Manager → the drive → Policies). Turn that off first, or keep the drive connected and powered until it has finished.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_IssueSpace">Less than 3% of the drive is free — free up some space first.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_IssueNtfs">Arranging files works on NTFS drives only.</system:String>

    <!-- Defrag: SMR drives -->
    <system:String x:Key="Defrag_AdviceSmr">This drive records in overlapping (SMR) tracks: it slows down sharply while writing a lot, so a full defragmentation can take many hours. Windows doesn't take that into account — prefer "Arrange program files", which moves only what programs load.</system:String>

    <!-- Cleaner: CapCut -->
    <system:String x:Key="CleanCat_CapCut_Title">CapCut: old versions and caches</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="CleanCat_CapCut_Desc">Every old CapCut version it keeps after updating (about 1.5–1.8 GB each — only the current one runs), plus its caches wherever its settings put them: effects, images, proxy videos, pre-renders, its built-in browser cache and logs. Your projects, presets, screen recordings and materials are never touched.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="CleanCat_CapCut_Warn">Close CapCut to clean its caches (old versions are removed even while it runs). Effects you use are downloaded again the next time, and proxy videos are rebuilt.</system:String>

